---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../../styles/giveaway.css';
import { RULES_VERSION, SITE_ORIGIN, BAN_LADDER_DAYS } from '../../data/giveawayConfig.js';

const [d1, d2, d3] = BAN_LADDER_DAYS;
const toc = [
  ['s1', 'Scope'], ['s2', 'No affiliation'], ['s3', 'Eligibility'], ['s4', 'Free entry'], ['s5', 'How to enter'], ['s6', 'Proof and temporary images'],
  ['s7', 'Checks and review'], ['s8', 'Extra tickets'], ['s9', 'Prohibited conduct'], ['s10', 'Penalties'], ['s11', 'Choosing winners'],
  ['s12', 'Claiming a prize'], ['s13', 'Our safety commitments'], ['s14', 'Prizes and payment'], ['s15', 'Data and privacy'], ['s16', 'Changes and liability'], ['s17', 'Disputes']
];
const schema = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'Giveaway Official Rules', url: SITE_ORIGIN + '/giveaways/rules/', dateModified: RULES_VERSION };
---

<BaseLayout title="Giveaway Official Rules" description="The official rules for every FCMobiletools giveaway: eligibility, how to enter, review, penalties, fair winner selection and safe prize claiming.">
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script>
  <main class="gw-root" id="app">
    <div class="gw-aurora" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i></div>
    <div class="gw-wrap gw-narrow">
      <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="gw-note" style="margin-bottom:18px"><a href="/giveaways/" style="color:var(--gw-cyan)">Giveaways</a> / Official Rules</nav>
      <div class="gw-eyebrow"><i></i> Legal</div>
      <h1 class="gw-h1" style="font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,48px)">Giveaway Official Rules</h1>
      <p class="gw-lede">These Rules apply to every giveaway run on FCMobiletools. By entering you confirm that you have read them and agree to follow them. If you do not agree, do not enter.</p>
      <p class="gw-note" style="margin-top:12px">Version {RULES_VERSION}. These Rules replace all earlier versions. A giveaway is governed by the version that was in force when it opened.</p>
      <ul class="gw-toc">{toc.map(([id, t], i) => <li><a href={'#' + id}>{i + 1}. {t}</a></li>)}</ul>

      <div class="gw-prose">
        <h2 id="s1">1. Scope</h2>
        <p>These Rules are issued by FCMobiletools, operated by Tanzim FC (the "Organizer", "we", "us"), at fcmobiletools.online. Each giveaway has its own page that states the prize, the number of winners, the entry period and any extra requirements. Where a giveaway page conflicts with these Rules, the giveaway page controls for that giveaway only.</p>

        <h2 id="s2">2. No affiliation</h2>
        <p>Our giveaways are run independently. They are not sponsored, endorsed, administered by or associated with Electronic Arts, EA SPORTS FC Mobile, Apple, Google, YouTube, Discord or Instagram. All product names and marks belong to their owners. Those companies carry no responsibility for any giveaway.</p>

        <h2 id="s3">3. Eligibility</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>You must hold a registered FCMobiletools account with a verified email address.</li>
          <li>You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority where you live. If you are younger, you may take part only if a parent or legal guardian has read and accepted these Rules for you, and that adult is the person who confirms the prize and receives it.</li>
          <li>You may hold one account only. One person may have one entry per giveaway. Entries made through shared, borrowed, bought or automated accounts are void.</li>
          <li>The Organizer, its moderators, administrators, contractors and their immediate household members may not win.</li>
          <li>You may not take part if the law of the place where you live forbids you from entering or receiving the prize. You are responsible for checking this. The giveaway is void where prohibited.</li>
          <li>You may not take part while you are paused or removed under section 10.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s4">4. Free entry and no ad interaction</h2>
        <p><strong>No purchase is necessary.</strong> Every requirement is free to complete, and entering costs nothing. You are never required or encouraged to view, click or interact with any advertisement to enter, to gain tickets or to improve your chances. Any suggestion otherwise is false, and you should report it.</p>

        <h2 id="s5">5. How to enter</h2>
        <p>To enter, complete every requirement shown on the giveaway page before the entry period ends. For a standard giveaway these are:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Complete your FCMobiletools profile.</li>
          <li>Complete at least one survey on FCMobiletools.</li>
          <li>Complete at least one quest on FCMobiletools.</li>
          <li>Join the official Discord server and enter your exact Discord username.</li>
          <li>Subscribe to the YouTube channels @ashverseunited and @tanzimfc, and upload one screenshot for each subscription showing the Subscribed state.</li>
          <li>Accept these Rules when you submit.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>A giveaway page may add or change requirements before it opens. Requirements never change after a giveaway has opened. The entry period is shown on the giveaway page and is measured by our server clock. Late entries are not accepted.</p>

        <h2 id="s6">6. Proof screenshots and temporary images</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Each screenshot must be a genuine, unedited capture from your own account, taken for this giveaway. It must show the channel and the Subscribed state.</li>
          <li>You must use a different screenshot for each channel. Reusing one image for several requirements is not allowed.</li>
          <li>Screenshots are stored as temporary images that delete themselves automatically after the period shown on the giveaway page, which is 24 hours unless stated otherwise. Because of this, you may be asked to upload a screenshot again.</li>
          <li>If a screenshot expires or cannot be opened before an administrator reviews it, your entry moves to "corrected proof needed". You will have the time stated in the request to upload it again. If you do not, your entry is not eligible for the draw.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s7">7. Automated checks and human review</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Automated checks.</strong> When you submit, our system checks your profile, your survey and quest records, duplicate entries and whether each screenshot is available. Entries that pass are placed in the draw straight away on a provisional basis.</li>
          <li><strong>Human review.</strong> An administrator then approves your entry, rejects it, or asks you for a corrected screenshot. A provisional entry is not a guarantee that it will be approved.</li>
          <li><strong>Reasons and records.</strong> Every decision is recorded with a reason and a timestamp. You can see the full history of your entry in your account. We keep these records as evidence of how the giveaway was run.</li>
          <li><strong>Winners are reviewed before they are announced.</strong> No winner is announced until an administrator has approved that winner's entry.</li>
          <li>Our decisions on whether a requirement has been met are made in good faith and are final, subject to section 10.4.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s8">8. Extra tickets</h2>
        <p>Where a giveaway offers them, you may earn extra tickets by taking a free daily boost and by inviting friends who complete a valid entry using your personal link. Each giveaway page states the limits. Extra tickets improve your chances but never guarantee a win. Referral tickets are void if the invited entry is rejected, comes from the same network or device as yours, or is created by you or for you. Invitations may not be sent as spam.</p>

        <h2 id="s9">9. Prohibited conduct</h2>
        <p>The following are not allowed, and any of them may lead to the penalties in section 10:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Creating or using more than one account, or entering on behalf of another person.</li>
          <li>Submitting a fake, edited, borrowed, reused or misleading screenshot, or a false Discord username.</li>
          <li>Using bots, scripts, emulators for automation, or any tool that creates entries, completes surveys or quests, or manipulates tickets automatically.</li>
          <li>Hiding your identity or network in order to evade duplicate detection.</li>
          <li>Abusing referrals, including self-referral, fake sign-ups and paid or automated sign-ups.</li>
          <li>Impersonating the Organizer, an administrator or a winner, or pretending to hold a claim code.</li>
          <li>Trying to access, guess, copy or sell a claim code that is not yours.</li>
          <li>Harassing, threatening or deceiving staff or other entrants.</li>
          <li>Attempting to interfere with the website, the draw or the review process.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s10">10. Penalties</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Removal.</strong> If an administrator finds that you broke these Rules, or that a requirement was not truly completed, your entry is rejected or disqualified. Any prize connected to it is withdrawn, including a prize that was already announced.</li>
          <li><strong>Pause from all giveaways.</strong> Confirmed violations also pause your account from every giveaway for a set time, which means you will miss out on every giveaway that opens during that time. The pause increases with each confirmed violation: first violation, {d1} days; second violation, {d2} days; third violation, {d3} days; fourth violation, permanent. We may apply a longer or permanent pause at once for fraud, impersonation, use of bots, or abuse of a claim code.</li>
          <li><strong>Other action.</strong> We may also restrict or close the account in line with our Terms of Service, and we may report fraud to the platforms involved or to the authorities.</li>
          <li><strong>Review of a penalty.</strong> You may ask us to review a penalty by contacting us through the official handles on the Claim Safety page within 14 days of the decision. Include your username and any evidence. We will reply with a reason. The outcome of the review is final.</li>
          <li>A paused account may not take part in any giveaway, including through a new account. A new account created to avoid a pause is treated as a violation and the pause is extended.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s11">11. How winners are chosen</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Winners are chosen by a random draw from eligible entries after the entry period closes. Eligible entries are those in good standing: not rejected, not disqualified, not withdrawn, and not paused at the time of the draw.</li>
          <li><strong>Fair draw method.</strong> Before a giveaway opens, we publish a fingerprint (a cryptographic hash) of a secret seed. When the entry period closes, the list of eligible entries and their tickets is frozen and fingerprinted. The seed and the frozen list are combined to rank every entry. After the results are published, we reveal the seed so that anyone can repeat the draw and check that the result matches. We cannot change the seed after the fingerprint has been published.</li>
          <li>Each ticket is one chance. An entry with more tickets has proportionally more chances.</li>
          <li>The draw produces winners and ranked alternates. If a winner fails review, forfeits, cannot be verified or is disqualified, the prize passes to the next eligible entry in the same fixed ranking. This is a "reroll" and it follows the same published order.</li>
          <li>Some giveaways have community milestones. When the number of entries reaches a milestone shown on the giveaway page, the extra winners or prizes described there are unlocked. Milestones that are not reached do not apply.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s12">12. Claiming a prize</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Announcement.</strong> Winners are announced on the giveaway page using a masked name. You will see a prize notice in your account.</li>
          <li><strong>Secret claim code.</strong> Each winner receives a private claim code in their own account. The code is shown only to the winner. You must keep it secret and must not share it with anyone except an administrator on an official handle for the purpose of claiming.</li>
          <li><strong>How to claim.</strong> Sign in, save the Discord or Instagram handle you will contact us from, reveal your code, and send the code to our official Discord or Instagram handle within the claim period stated on the giveaway page. If no period is stated, it is 72 hours from the announcement.</li>
          <li><strong>Verification.</strong> Only an administrator can check a code. We pay a prize only when the code is valid and is sent from the handle you saved. If the handle does not match, or the code is invalid, we will not pay, and we may ask for further proof of identity.</li>
          <li><strong>Forfeit.</strong> If you do not claim in time, cannot be verified, or do not meet these Rules, you forfeit the prize and we may award it to the next eligible entry. We may extend a claim period at our discretion.</li>
          <li><strong>Lost or exposed codes.</strong> If you think someone else has seen your code, contact an official handle straight away. We may replace the code. A replaced code stops working. We are not responsible for a prize lost because you shared your code.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s13">13. Our safety commitments</h2>
        <p>We will never ask you for your password, card or bank login details, one-time codes, recovery codes or game account credentials. We will never ask you to pay a fee, a tax, a deposit or a "verification payment" to receive a prize. We will never ask you to click a link to receive a prize, other than the claim page on fcmobiletools.online. Official handles are listed on the Claim Safety page. Anyone who contacts you from another handle about a giveaway is not us. Report them to us.</p>

        <h2 id="s14">14. Prizes and payment</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>The prize and its value are stated on the giveaway page. Values are in the currency shown.</li>
          <li>Prizes are paid outside this website, using a method that we agree with the winner in a private conversation on an official handle. We choose from the methods that are available in the winner's country, and a prize may be paid in a different form of equal value if payment in the stated form is not possible.</li>
          <li>The winner is responsible for any bank, transfer, currency conversion or platform fees charged to the winner, and for any tax owed on the prize. We may ask for details that are needed to complete the payment, but never those listed in section 13.</li>
          <li>Prizes are not transferable, cannot be exchanged for something else at the winner's request, and have no cash alternative unless we say so.</li>
          <li>Where a winner is a minor, payment is made to the parent or legal guardian.</li>
          <li>We record each payment, and we may show a payment proof on the Winners hall with the winner's name masked.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s15">15. Data and privacy</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>To run a giveaway we use the information in your account and the details you give us: your username, profile fields, survey and quest records, your Discord username, your screenshots, and the handle you use to claim.</li>
          <li>To detect duplicate and abusive entries we create a one-way, scrambled identifier from your network address and store it with your entry. We do not store the address itself for this purpose and we do not use the identifier for advertising.</li>
          <li>Screenshots are temporary and delete themselves, as described in section 6. We keep entry decisions, penalties and payment records for as long as we need them to run the giveaway, to settle disputes and to stop repeat abuse, and then delete or anonymise them.</li>
          <li>Winners are shown publicly only with a masked username. By claiming a prize you agree to this limited publicity. We never publish your contact handle or payment details.</li>
          <li>Our <a href="/legal/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> applies to all of this information.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s16">16. Changes, cancellation and liability</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>We may correct errors, pause, change or cancel a giveaway if it cannot run as planned because of fraud, a technical fault, legal risk, a security problem or any cause outside our control. We will say so on the giveaway page. If we cancel a giveaway before the draw, no prize is awarded.</li>
          <li>We are not responsible for entries that are late, lost, incomplete or not received because of problems with your device, connection, email, third-party platforms or the temporary image host.</li>
          <li>To the fullest extent the law allows, the Organizer is not liable for any loss, damage, injury or cost connected with a giveaway or a prize, except where the law does not allow that limit. Nothing in these Rules limits any right you have that cannot be limited by law.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="s17">17. Disputes and general</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>If you have a concern, contact us first through the official handles or the <a href="/legal/contact">contact page</a>, and we will try to resolve it in good faith.</li>
          <li>These Rules are governed by the law of the place where the Organizer operates, and any dispute that cannot be settled in good faith is for the courts of that place, unless the law of your home country gives you a right to a different forum that cannot be waived.</li>
          <li>If a part of these Rules cannot be enforced, the rest stays in force. Our failure to enforce a rule is not a waiver of it.</li>
          <li>We may update these Rules. A new version applies to giveaways that open after it is published. We will always show the version and date at the top of this page.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <p class="gw-note" style="margin-top:40px"><a href="/giveaways/" style="color:var(--gw-cyan)">Back to giveaways</a> · <a href="/giveaways/safety/" style="color:var(--gw-cyan)">Claim Safety guide</a></p>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
